  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/app/src/setup_align.rs`: `generation_problem` no longer refuses area controls in an aligned setup. The refusal applied to the four verified 2D kinds: Face, 2D Contour, 2D Pocket and 2D Adaptive. One change fixes all four.\n- The area law already reads each world value in the setup frame: the picked faces and edges (`selection_geometry_in`), the stitched open chains, the part material and its silhouette (`setup_align::facets_in`) and the heights. The stock outline is furniture and stays unaligned, as in #326. Thus no second transform is added. A second transform would turn the picks two times.\n- The tilt refusal and the refusal of the unverified kinds stay.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/2210-aligned-area-controls.md`.\n\n## Readings and pinning tests\n\nNew file `crates/app/tests/setup_align_2d_area.rs`. The part is an L with unequal arms. Setup1 turns it 90 degrees about Z (`AlignPreset::TurnZ90`). The turned L, the L as modelled and the L turned -90 degrees are three different regions. Each case generates in the aligned document and in a document with the turn baked into the mesh. Each case asserts:\n- the two paths agree to 1e-6 mm, and the two posted programs are equal;\n- no warning blocks the post, the program stock simulation finds 0 gouge cells, and the setup posts.\n\nCases:\n- `turned_adaptive2d_excludes_the_picked_face_where_the_part_lies` and `turned_pocket2d_excludes_the_picked_face_where_the_part_lies`: an exclude boundary of the picked top face. The feed passes (sampled each 0.25 mm) stay a tool radius off the turned L. They reach (8, 15), which is inside the modelled L and inside the -90 L.\n- `turned_face_clears_the_band_of_the_turned_pick`: Face refuses an exclude boundary by its own law, so the case uses a 1 mm offset. The band reaches Y 23 and stays in X [4 - r, 26 + r].\n- `turned_contour2d_offset_rides_the_turned_outline`: the ride stays r + 1 off the turned L and passes beside the turned long arm at X 28.\n- `as_modelled_area_controls_never_meet_the_aligned_door`: an unaligned setup gets no refusal.\n\nUpdated: `opframe_picks::tilt_times_picks_and_unverified_stay_refused_and_area_passes_in_phase_two`, `setup_align_3d::enabling_aligned_3d_keeps_tilt_refused_and_passes_2d_area`.\n\nGate: these suites pass in debug: `setup_align_2d_area`, `opframe_picks`, `setup_align_3d`, `setup_align`, `area_controls`, `area_open`, `area_picks`, `area_chains`, `area_overhead`, `open_band`, `opframe_seam`, `align_axes`, `align_compose`, `plane_align`, `points_align`, `winding_align`, and the `camcraft-app` lib tests. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean. The full quick gate selected all suites for this diff; I did not run that full set.\n\n## Posted G-code and goldens\n\nAn unaligned setup does not change: `generation_problem` returns early when the setup has no alignment, and no generator code changed. No golden file changes. An aligned setup with area controls now posts where it was refused before.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No run on a real control.\n- The fig8 reproduction from the issue was not generated in the GUI by me. A release build of this head is given to the maintainer for that check.\n- `boundary_picks::extend_to_loop` (a UI helper that picks the most horizontal face) reads face normals without the setup frame. For a turn about Z the result is the same. For a flip or a free angle it can select a different face. It only seeds a selection and does not cut. This is not changed here.\n- Tilted planes and the unverified kinds stay refused.\n\nChangelog: 2D Adaptive, 2D Pocket, 2D Contour and Face now accept area controls (boundaries, offset, containment) in a setup that holds the part turned; before, generation refused them.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2210\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
